# Brand color on light surfaces

Accent `#D4FF00` looks poor on white / near-white. **Never** use it on light sections.

## On light / white (`tone="light"`, `--section-light`, pale backgrounds)

- Use **black** (`#0A0A0A` / `foreground`) and **greys** only (muted, opacity steps)
- Display type: `font-pixel-circle` for titles / numbers — still allowed
- Eyebrows / labels: mono uppercase in grey
- Dividers, marks, bullets, underlines, watermarks: black or grey — **not** accent
- No lime tint washes, lime borders, or lime decorative pixels

## Where accent is allowed

- Dark heroes / dark sections (`bg-black`, `--section-dark`)
- CTAs on dark (lime button + dark text)
- GlyphMatrix / shader accents on dark

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — light timeline / stats / clients
<span className="bg-accent" />
<span className="text-accent/20">4</span>

// ✅ GOOD — light surfaces
<span className="bg-foreground" />
<span className="text-foreground/15">4</span>
```
